  "task": {
    "objective": "Roles 0/1 coordinate to deliver the parcel through one of two exits; roles 2/3 coordinate to intercept. Scouts provide expiring route intelligence and operate corridor gates.",
    "natural_termination": "Interceptor action 7 within Manhattan distance one of the courier captures the parcel; otherwise courier action 7 on either exit delivers it. Capture has explicit priority if both triggers occur. Horizon 80 truncates as an unresolved draw.",
    "interaction": "Scouts can traverse closed gates, cache local gate/opponent facts and explicitly relay them. A teammate gains access to those facts, while opponents near the transmitter can intercept the same report. Gate toggles change others' movement; public lures can redirect behavior but are never ground-truth contacts.",
    "observation_access": "Radar-style local sensing has Manhattan radius three for scouts and one for main roles, without wall occlusion. Only scouts see their own notebook. A radio message is accessible to its team and roles within radius two at the actual broadcast, until TTL expires. Public map reveals gate sites only. Unverified lures and public terminal outcome are separated from actual locally observed contacts."
  },
